WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.857
How exactly would 3D printers 
build a habitat&nbsp;on Mars?

00:00:04.209 --> 00:00:07.218
If we leverage autonomous robotics,

00:00:07.218 --> 00:00:10.919
we'll send 3D printers and other 
construction&nbsp;robots

00:00:10.919 --> 00:00:14.425
to build protective habitats and shelters

00:00:14.425 --> 00:00:17.499
before the crew even arrives.

00:00:17.499 --> 00:00:21.835
These structures&nbsp;are manufactured 
layer by layer by layer.

00:00:21.835 --> 00:00:27.739
And as construction progresses, prebuilt and&nbsp;
preintegrated hardware like airlocks

00:00:27.739 --> 00:00:30.786
or life support equipment brought from Earth

00:00:30.786 --> 00:00:37.481
are&nbsp;inserted into the print until finally 
they're sealed at various connection points.

00:00:37.481 --> 00:00:41.441
We also&nbsp;want to incorporate practical 
architectural elements such as

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:44.838
access to natural&nbsp;light through windows and greenery.

00:00:44.838 --> 00:00:51.259
Which we know are critical to positive&nbsp;
psychological functioning and well-being.

